      "title": "Overview"
    },
    {
      "description": "A lens is a structure (often an object or function) that pairs a getter and a non-mutating setter for some other data structure.\nHaving the pair of get and set for a given data structure enables a few key features.\nLenses are also composable. This allows easy immutable updates to deeply nested data.\nOther implementations:",
      "items": [
        {
          "node_type": "item",
          "title": "partial.lenses",
          "description": "Tasty syntax sugar and a lot of powerful features",
          "children": [],
